 and closer  to the epic conclusion  of the entire series and that in itself  is big news  and a big deal quick warning from this  point on in the video i will be  discussing  mha manga spoilers so proceed with  caution  you have been warned so the big question  now is what can we expect from the final  act  of the story with deku deciding to leave  the ua  before becoming a full-fledged hero the  story of my hero academia  is ironically moving away from the  academia  itself although to be fair deku could  always  change his mind and return and we could  also see the story checking in on the  other students who are still at ua  so i think it's still premature to say  that the ua will no longer be an  important part of the story  the last few arcs in the manga have been  by far the best arcs in the entire  series  in my opinion so i'm extremely excited  to see  where the story will go from here way  back in june of 2020 i made a video  addressing rumors  about the war arc potentially being the  final arc  in the story i can totally understand  why so many people were speculating that  the war arc might be the end  so many crazy things ended up happening  in this  most recent arcs so much changed so  quickly and the entire hero society  basically collapsed  i can't blame anyone for thinking that  this could be the build-up to some sort  of climactic  end but as i said back in that video at  the time  i did not believe that this war arc  would be the final  arc i believed that there would be more  arcs to come  but i did say that the war arc would  change everything we thought we knew  about boku no hero and i said that after  this arc  things would never be the same again  once the arc  did come to a conclusion many months  later that is exactly what happened  with the hero society collapsing the  massive villain prison breaks  and deku leaving the ua things will  definitely  never be the same again so what will  happen  now unless deku changes his mind and  returns 