xisted before the war arc has  basically collapsed  and ever since the tartarus prison break  first happened  i've been saying here on the channel  that stain is not going to be fighting  on the side of the villains  now that most of the opportunistic  half-hearted and self-centered heroes  have already retired  and now that the hero society itself has  practically crumbled  stains biggest problem won't be the  heroes  not anymore in his own twisted way stain  truly believes  in the ideal of heroism so i predict  that he will actually start fighting as  a vigilante to protect the people of  japan from villain attacks  in fact we might even get a deku stain  team  up sometime in the future stain already  acknowledged deku as a true hero worthy  of respect  so stain would probably have no problem  fighting side by side with deku and  don't get me wrong i don't think deku  will ever become friends with stain  deku will not simply forget the terrible  things that stain has done  but if the situation calls for it and  they are facing a common enemy  i could totally see vigilante stain and  vigilante deku  fighting together against the villains i  don't know about you guys but that is  something that i would freaking  love to see and speaking of the villains  we can expect them to only keep getting  stronger  in this final act i mean sure some of  the villains that escaped from prison  will just go off on their own and do  their own thing  but all for one is smart and i am sure  that he is going to gather the strongest  villains who escaped into his  own private army orchestrating six  additional prison breaks alongside the  tartarus prison break  wasn't just a random distraction tactic  you better believe that it was also a  recruitment  tactic and don't even get me started on  how strong shigaraki may possibly become  if all for one succeeds in completing  ujjiko's previously interrupted  procedure  so yeah the final act of the story is  going to be  insane the villains will be stronger  than ever before  the hero society will be in complete  chaos  deku may end up being a vigilante  alongside stain we may see  overpowered international heroes coming  to japan to help to fight against the  villains  and so much more we might even finally  figure out who the freaking ua traitor  is  remember that huge plot point from  earlier on in the story  nope that still hasn't been resolved  anyway let me know what you guys are  expecting to see in the final act and  how long do you think that this act  will last my guess is that the manga  will continue for at least another two  to three years because it is extremely  popular  and profitable and who knows maybe even  after the main story ends we're going to  get some kind of sequel like  mha the next generation or boku no hero  shipuden  man there is so much crazy potential so  i can't wait  to see how this final act is going to  unfold  don't forget to leave your thoughts down  in the comments  is deku going to become a vigilante and  maybe even team up  with stain do you think that we might  get a time skip  sometime in the near future will we ever  find  the ua trader let me know down below  if you enjoyed this video you want to  see more boku no hero content right here  on the channel please leave a like to  let me know it really does help  and if you are new to anime opera or  maybe you watch our videos but you  haven't subscribed yet  please make this the video do you  subscribe and hit that notification bell  to turn on  all notifications you can also hit me up  on twitter  and instagram at anime opera  thanks again to ragnarok labyrinth for  sponsoring this video  check them out link in the description  as always thank you guys so much for  watching  and until next time see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you

